---

<BaseLayout title="Resume — Dan Maas" description="Dan Maas — Software Shepherd · Agentic AI · AWS · Cloudflare. Resume and professional experience." activeLink="">
  <!--
    The outer wrapper provides the full-viewport background in the browser but
    is intentionally OUTSIDE #resume-capture so the PDF only captures actual
    content height. With `min-h-screen` previously on #resume-capture, every
    PDF page ended with a tall blank area at the bottom (the wrapper forcing a
    viewport-tall canvas while the real content was much shorter).
  -->
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-base-200">
    <!-- PDF capture area: everything inside here is rendered to the PDF -->
    <div id="resume-capture" class="bg-base-200">
    <!-- Header banner -->
    <div class="bg-base-300 border-b border-base-content/10">
      <div class="px-6 py-8 md:px-12">
        <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-between gap-6">
